The AirPlay 2 protocol logic in this package — HAP pair-setup and its SRP-6a
parameters, the binary-plist message shapes, the PTP grandmaster's message
layouts and announce dataset, the realtime RTP framing and its encryption, and
the anchor packet — is a TypeScript port of the Apache-2.0 licensed sources in
that project's `src/` directory (ap2_hap.c, ap2_ptp.c, ap2_client.c, ap2_plist.c
and ap2_bplist.cpp).

Those files carry per-file `SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0` headers and are
explicitly reusable under that licence on their own. The GPL parts of cliairplay
— its `cliairplay.c` entry point and the libraop RAOP core it links — are NOT
used here: this package contains no AirPlay 1 / RAOP code and links no native
libraries.

The ALAC frame layout was read from libraop's decoder (alac.c) to establish what
receivers accept; no decoder code is included.
